## 9. Quick Command Reference

| Task | Command or option |
|---|---|
| TCP SYN scan | `nmap -sS TARGET_IP` |
| TCP Connect scan | `nmap -sT TARGET_IP` |
| UDP scan | `sudo nmap -sU TARGET_IP` |
| Scan specific ports | `nmap -p22,80,443 TARGET_IP` |
| Scan a port range | `nmap -p1-1023 TARGET_IP` |
| Scan all TCP ports | `nmap -p- TARGET_IP` |
| Scan 100 common ports | `nmap -F TARGET_IP` |
| Scan the top 10 ports | `nmap --top-ports 10 TARGET_IP` |
| Scan ports in numerical order | `nmap -r TARGET_IP` |
| Use normal timing | `nmap -T3 TARGET_IP` |
| Use faster timing | `nmap -T4 TARGET_IP` |
| Set maximum packet rate | `nmap --max-rate 50 TARGET_IP` |
| Request a minimum packet rate | `nmap --min-rate 15 TARGET_IP` |
| Set maximum parallelism | `nmap --max-parallelism 20 TARGET_IP` |

Replace `TARGET_IP` with the address of a system you own or are explicitly authorized to scan.

